35:We  also  accessed  the  Norwegian  National  Registry for healthcare information about all enrolled patients at baseline. This allowed us to access dates and durations of  contacts  with  the  Norwegian  healthcare  system  for ICD-10 F-01-09 labeled events (Mental, Behavioral and Neurodevelopmental disorders) in the follow-up period (e.g.,  from  the  start  of  treatment  to  10-year  follow-up) for all participants, serving as a proxy for illness severity.
75:## Results
79:A total of 218 healthy CTRL and 79 patients were included  in  the  longitudinal  analysis  (table  1  and  supplementary  figures  1  and  8).  There  was  no  significant difference  either  in  the  number  of  contacts  with  the healthcare system for ICD-10 classified 'Mental, Behavioral  and  Neurodevelopmental  disorders,'  nor  in duration of contacts with the healthcare system (e.g., the duration of treatment) between the longitudinal sample and the drop-outs. There was no significant association between  attrition  groups  and  PANSS  scores,  or  median  cortical  deviation  scores.  Data  on  medication  use for  each  timepoint  showed that patients primarily used second-generation antipsychotics (62% at baseline, 48% at 1 year, and 17% at 10 years) or did not use any antipsychotics (38%, 50%, and 83%, respectively; for details, see supplementary material).
173:Fig. 6. Results from the LME model testing for associations between symptom scores and cortical deviations (equation 2). We report man effects for the PANSS total domain (A), the PANSS general domain (B), PANSS negative symptoms (C), and a significant interaction in a single region between the PANSS negative scores and follow-up time (D). The color bar shows the effects size of each effect.
